==Freedom of panorama== <!--T:33-->
</translate>
<noinclude>{{CRT shortcut|FOP|Philippines}}</noinclude>
<translate>
<!--T:34-->
{{NotMark}} for majority of the works of art.</translate> {{tl|NoFoP-Philippines}}
<translate>
<!--T:74-->
'''Note:''' Please tag Philippine no-FoP deletion requests: <tvar name=nofopcode><code><nowiki><noinclude>[[Category:Philippine FOP cases/pending]]</noinclude></nowiki></code></tvar>

<!--T:66-->
There is no provision in any of the exceptions listed under Chapter VIII ("Limitations on copyright") of the ''IP Code of the Philippines (Act No. 8293) (2015 Edition)'' allowing images of copyrighted architectural and artistic works permanently located in public spaces to be made and/or distributed for commercial purposes, such as post cards, calendars, advertising materials, travel guides and brochures, website development, vlogs, and mobile/web applications.{{sref|8293/2015 Chapter VIII Section 184–190}}

<!--T:59-->
According to Atty. Chuck Valerio, chief of the Bureau of Copyright and Related Rights of the Intellectual Property Office (IPOPHL), in 2021, the absence of this exception means it is infringing to use shots of a building authored by an architect who is a National Artist in a video to be marketed to Netflix. Whether the appearance of the building or monument in the image is intentional or not (that is, whether as main subject or as {{pg|Commons:De minimis|incidental inclusion}}) does not make any difference.<tvar name="ref"><ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.philstar.com/business/2021/11/28/2144241/changing-landscape-copyright |title=Changing landscape of copyright |date=2021-11-28 |last=Reyes |first=Mary Ann LL. |work=Philippine Star |accessdate=2024-01-10}}</ref></tvar>

<!--T:54-->
Section 184 of Chapter VIII provides the following acts as not constituting copyright infringement:{{sref|8293/2015 Chapter VIII Section 184.1}}
</translate>

{{quote|<translate><!--T:55-->
(d) The reproduction and communication to the public of literary, scientific or artistic works as part of reports of current events by means of photography, cinematography or broadcasting to the extent necessary for the purpose; (Sec. 12, P.D. No. 49)
(e) The inclusion of a work in a publication, broadcast, or other communication to the public, sound recording or film, if such inclusion is made by way of illustration for teaching purposes and is compatible with fair use: ''Provided'', That the source and of the name of the author, if appearing in the work, are mentioned.</translate>}}

<translate>
<!--T:56-->
None of these provisions are strictly free enough for Wikimedia Commons. In particular, {{pg|1=Commons:Fair use|2=fair use is not allowed}} on Wikimedia Commons, and licensing limited to noncommercial uses is not allowed either.

